      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruitland%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The arrival of the railroad after the Civil War shifted development toward the tracks, reshaping the town’s layout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityoffruitland.com/how_do_i_/learn_about_find/history.php"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fruitland City Hall now sits on the very spot that once marked Disharoon’s Cross Roads, preserving the town’s original crossroads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityoffruitland.com/how_do_i_/learn_about_find/history.php"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Until 1867 the village straddled Somerset and Worcester Counties, making it politically split until Wicomico County was created.",
